 "The list": "",
 "At the bottom of Zeno’s spring: a bronze plate with the same list of names as Nico’s machine screen. Seven of them lit. The parts follow the list.": "",
 "Zeno of Elea": "",
 "Student of Parmenides, famous for his paradoxes of motion: the dichotomy (to arrive you must first go halfway, forever), Achilles and the tortoise, the arrow frozen in each instant, the stadium. They defend Parmenides: if motion leads to contradictions, perhaps motion is an illusion. The modern answer uses infinite series that add up to a finite sum; Diogenes answered by getting up and walking.": "",
